  "response_complete": true,
  "response_text": "It's important to address any concerns about vaginal discharge and irritation promptly. Here are some steps you can take:\n\n1. **Consult a Healthcare Professional**: The first step is to see a healthcare provider, such as a gynecologist or a primary care physician. They can provide a proper diagnosis and recommend appropriate treatment.\n\n2. **Avoid Irritants**: If you suspect that certain products or activities are causing irritation, avoid them. This might include harsh soaps, douches, or certain types of underwear.\n\n3. **Maintain Good Hygiene**: Keep the area clean and dry. Avoid using scented products in the genital area.\n\n4. **Change Your Lifestyle**: Sometimes, changes in diet, exercise, or stress levels can affect vaginal health. Consider these factors and make adjustments if necessary.\n\n5. **Follow Treatment Instructions**: If you are prescribed medication, take it as directed. Do not stop taking it without consulting your healthcare provider.\n\n6. **Monitor Symptoms**: Keep track of any changes in your symptoms and report them to your healthcare provider.\n\n7. **Consider Risk Reduction**: If you have a history of sexually transmitted infections (STIs), be sure to discuss this with your healthcare provider. They can provide guidance on how to reduce the risk of reinfection.\n\nRemember, it's important to address these issues promptly to prevent complications.",
